[SetUp "1"]

1. Nd2 { However, the strong reply of } 1... Qc6
{ solves Black's problems; thanks to the threat of mate on g2, Black has sufficient time to save the rook, for example: }
2. e4 Rxc3
{ Yet another example of how time and geometry are the fundamental building blocks of chess tactics. }
