{ @@HeaderStart@@Double Check@@HeaderEnd@@  Double check is a type of discovered check where one piece moves to give check and uncovers another piece that also attacks the king. Needless to say this is a bombshell and two out of the three possible ways of defending the king no longer apply: it is not possible to interpose with a piece, as check arrives from two directions; you cannot capture the checking piece because there are two of them. The only remaining hope is to move the king to a safe square, presuming there is one… }
1. Bc6#
{ In the above position White ends the game with the killing 1. Bc6#. The king's two escape squares are controlled by the two attacking pieces. It is amusing to note that both the checking pieces are hanging, but because of the power of a double check they are immune from capture. }
*

